{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"LEAF 0880 — reports (a)(b)(c) + ADR 0110 WRITTEN.\n\nVERIFIED THE HEADLINE MYSELF before publishing rather than trusting the research agent: re-derived\nthe files-vs-LOC control from the raw artifacts with my own code. Exact match on every figure —\nfiles bands 22.7/40.2/46.0/63.5/58.6 (n=2194), control at fixed LOC 41.6/48.2/62.2, control at fixed\nfiles 34.5/45.8/41.1 (non-monotonic). Also re-ran analyse_a.py and it reproduced the ticket-level\ntables identically, which is AC2's reproducibility requirement.\nNOTE on my first verification attempt: it returned zeros for every files band because I guessed the\nwrong field name (files_touched vs the actual 'files'). Worth recording — a verification that\nsilently returns zeros looks like a refutation. I checked the record keys and re-ran.\n\nDECISION RECORDED (ADR 0110, .numbers/0110 claimed, gen_adr_index regenerated, bijection check\npasses): change shape enters the floor as an ADVISORY on FILE SURFACE; a line-count floor does NOT.\n - files predicts (effect survives the LOC control); LOC does not (dissolves under the files control)\n - advisory not blocking: all rho <= 0.42, worst stratum still 62%, so ~38% false-positive rate\n - commit fragmentation DROPPED: 90.1% of tickets are single-commit; Gerrit amend-and-repush puts\n   rework in patchsets, and its one correlation is reverse causation\n - the shipped bug-fix 150-line gate is untouched; what is declined is a NEW all-work line rule\n - nonstationary: re-tune, never freeze\n\n9ca8 FOURTH REMEDIATION (three blocks so far, every finding correct):\n - E4 x2: AC15/AC16 claimed verification by the module-size gate and the complexity ratchet, but BOTH\n   scan src/rebar only (module_size_support walks SRC_ROOT; PRODUCTION_SCOPE='src/rebar') while every\n   module this ships is under scripts/. The ACs claimed verification that could not happen. Now\n   asserted by the ticket's own suite instead.\n - G6: the baseline key was not section-qualified, and allow_insecure is an _as_bool key in BOTH\n   reconciler and jira — two definition sites would collapse into one entry, contradicting the\n   one-site-one-entry pillar. Names for config_key/feature_flag are now <section>.<key>.\nADMISSION-CAP FRICTION WORTH RECORDING: hit the 8,000-char plan-review admission cap FIVE times\n(9838 -> 8116 -> 8374 -> 8319 -> 8136 -> 8090 -> 7846). review-plan REFUSES admission above it, so\neach round of added rigour had to be paid for by cutting prose. The gate's own advice is to move\nindependent work into child tickets; declined this late because new children would need their own\nreviews and would hold the parent open. This ticket is genuinely larger than its five siblings.\nReview #4 running.\n\nDISPATCHED: fold the all-work analysis into scripts/backtest_bugfix_size.py so the reports reproduce\nfrom the REPO, not from scratch files (AC2+AC7), keeping the imported-shipped-predicate anti-drift\nproperty and staying offline (the Gerrit half needs credentials and stays documented-with-auth)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788321790671818001,"uuid":"b8d64438-fc83-4118-81be-9b4c557a416f"}